<article class="env-lemma" id="09CW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09CW">Lemma <span data-tag="09CW">18.34.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{O}_1 \to \mathcal{O}_2$ be a homomorphism of sheaves of rings. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_2$-modules. There is a canonical short exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \Omega _{\mathcal{O}_2/\mathcal{O}_1} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_2} \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{P}^1_{\mathcal{O}_2/\mathcal{O}_1}(\mathcal{F}) \to \mathcal{F} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> functorial in $\mathcal{F}$ called the <em>sequence of principal parts</em>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from the commutative algebra version (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/09CN" data-tag="09CN">10.133.6</a>) and Lemmas <a href="/tag/08TP" data-tag="08TP">18.33.4</a> and <a href="/tag/09CV" data-tag="09CV">18.34.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>